# QA Response Review (Project-Wide)

Every Cursor agent session runs lifecycle hooks under `.cursor/hooks/`. The `stop` orchestrator may inject `[QA_RESPONSE_REVIEW]` for a one-shot editorial pass.

## When you see `[QA_RESPONSE_REVIEW]`

This is **not** a new user task. Apply **`10-src/TOKEN-SAVING-AGENT-MANIFEST.md`** read-only against the draft.

### Required behavior

1. **Read-only** — do not call tools, edit files, run shell commands, or spawn subagents.
2. **Apply manifest tags** — `[H-CONTEXT]`, `[H-ZERO-TRUST]`, `[H-OBSERVE]`, `[OOP-*]`, `[PATCH-*]`, `[TRACE-*]`, PASS_3, `[REPORT-FORMAT]` when applicable.
3. **Output only** the final polished response — no meta-commentary.
4. **Preserve intent** — fix gaps without changing the user's goal or adding unrequested scope.
5. **Expand on violation** — full rules in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` when a tag fails.

### Subagents

Task/subagent runs use the same hook on `subagentStop`. Same read-only manifest rules.

### Opt-out

`QA_REVIEW_HOOK_ENABLED=false` disables the hook. `TOKEN_SAVING_MANIFEST_ENABLED=false` skips manifest injection at `sessionStart`.
